["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iscc", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Content Code (ISCC)](https://iscc.io/) is a content-derived identifier standardized by [ISO 24138](https://www.iso.org/standard/77899.html) for identifying digital assets. ISCC can be used in conjunction with other schemes, such as DOI, ISAN, ISBN, ISRC, ISSN and ISWC. A standard ISCC-CODE is build from multiple ISCC-UNITs. Each unit serve a different purpose. An ISCC-CODE typically look like `ISCC:KACT4EBWK27737D2AYCJRAL5Z36G76RFRMO4554RU26HZ4ORJGIVHDI`.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N2750e6ce71d74f2289219e91a650ee12", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "_:Nbc309b1e8c904b0db7fee66a45b76ee3", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/HashAlgorithm/sha3_256", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "sha3_256", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/Snippet", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:N90ec12ef1e7d4b3fb7b554c71e2c3e31", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/createdBy", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The `from` Element's Action or DefinedProcess is createdBy `to` Agent(s).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nda7f900a383f472a917f7470477b270e", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/autonomous", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:Nd5d16c92b67d4133b631da65199db9d6", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "_:N53e8ee55d64d4e6e88b7d89fa6aa87e0", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/HashAlgorithm", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A mathematical algorithm that maps data of arbitrary size to a bit string.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/ancestorOf", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/plannedInspectionLocation", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The planned location that a good, product or material is inspected.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
